  "id": "thresholds-and-expectation-thresholds",
  "title": "Thresholds and expectation thresholds",
  "description": "OpenAI's proof (2026) of the second Kahn–Kalai conjecture: the threshold for G(n,p) to contain a copy of a graph H is at most a universal constant times p_E(n,H)(1 + log₂ e(H)), where p_E is the least density at which every subgraph of H has at least ½ expected copies. The course proves planted resampling for spread families, a tree covering theorem that contains the spread lemma, and the construction of a tree of conditional extensions of H.",
